{
 "scope": "The codimension-m critical slicing for the part of the critical set where the DERIVATIVE VANISHES, and the coarea formula it extends to the whole space under the hypothesis that the derivative vanishes wherever it fails to be surjective. NOT the full critical set when m is at least 2, and NOT any Sard theorem; the gap is EXHIBITED by a counterexample rather than asserted. No hole migrated. The log-concave Cheeger-Buser line belongs to collaborator Wang Haocheng and was not touched.",
 "head": "34b92695ece4f636a1a7f1eafbbf41c685ee0348",
 "origin_main": "34b92695ece4f636a1a7f1eafbbf41c685ee0348",
 "incoming_receipt": "build/verification/20260917T034956.058840Z/report.json",
 "incoming_snapshot": "e87a9add07bbc20692efd7891719dcf6b8cdf6d1bf027fe3f36fd05b7f90b019",
 "incoming_entries": 566,
 "incoming_replayed_modules": 214,
 "incoming_workspace_drift": [],
 "new_declarations": [
  "Analysis.isClosed_zeroDeriv",
  "Analysis.exists_lipschitzOnWith_zeroDeriv_cover",
  "Analysis.ae_hausdorffMeasure_zeroDeriv_ball_eq_zero",
  "Analysis.ae_hausdorffMeasure_zeroDeriv_inter_levelSet_eq_zero",
  "Analysis.ae_hausdorffNormalized_zeroDeriv_inter_levelSet_eq_zero",
  "Analysis.isOpen_coareaJacobian_ne_zero",
  "Analysis.coarea_of_contDiff_of_critical_eq_zeroDeriv"
 ],
 "main_results": {
  "zero_derivative_slices": "for a C1 map into an m-dimensional target with m at least 1, almost every level meets the set where the derivative vanishes in an H^(n-m)-null set; the scalar argument verbatim, with the codimension-m Eilenberg bound whose constant epsilon^m tends to 0 precisely because m is at least 1",
  "why_m_positive_is_a_real_hypothesis": "with a zero-dimensional target every derivative vanishes, so that set is the whole space and its slices are the whole slices",
  "coarea_extension": "under the hypothesis that the derivative vanishes wherever it fails to be surjective, the regular-case coarea formula extends to the whole space: measurability comes from the previous round's unconditional slice measurability, and the critical contribution vanishes on both sides"
 },
 "scalar_consistency": {
  "automatic_for_m_one": "for a real differential, non-surjective and zero are the same condition, so the dichotomy hypothesis is automatic",
  "scalar_L10": "KLS.ae_surfaceMeasure_critical_inter_levelSet_eq_zero recovered verbatim",
  "scalar_L11": "KLS.coarea_of_contDiff recovered verbatim",
  "honest_difference": "both recoveries carry an extra 1 <= finrank V, as in the previous rounds, because the codimension-m statements assume fibre dimension plus codimension equals ambient dimension"
 },
 "the_gap_is_exhibited_not_asserted": {
  "what_is_missing": "for m at least 2 the coarea critical set is where the rank drops below m, which is STRICTLY LARGER than the vanishing-derivative set",
  "witness": "VectorCriticalSliceAudit.rank_deficient_witness: the rank-one orthogonal projection of the plane onto its first axis has derivative NOWHERE ZERO and NOWHERE SURJECTIVE, so the vanishing-derivative set is empty while the coarea critical set is everything, and the dichotomy hypothesis fails at every point",
  "why_the_method_does_not_extend": "the argument rests on u being epsilon-Lipschitz on the partition pieces, which needs the derivative to VANISH, not merely to be non-surjective"
 },
 "is_not": [
  "NO Sard theorem: nothing is claimed about the measure of the set of critical VALUES, which for a merely C1 map may well be positive",
  "NOT the general codimension-m coarea formula: the rank-deficient part is not covered",
  "KLS/Geometry/CriticalSlice.lean and KLS/Geometry/SmoothCoarea.lean were NOT modified; the codimension-m versions are parallel new modules",
  "nothing about sharp finite-regularity Sard, the two Cheeger comparisons or the five Energy holes"
 ],
 "remaining_work": [
  "the RANK-DEFICIENT part is the only remaining structural gap of the codimension-m coarea formula",
  "a possible route: stratify by rank, push the image of each stratum near an r-dimensional affine subspace by the approximating partition, and use the Eilenberg bound along the surviving m - r directions - but this needs simultaneous slicing along the r good directions, that is ITERATED SLICING, which is the hard part of the degenerate case of Federer's coarea formula and for which neither this repository nor Mathlib has tools",
  "a route-exploration round is recommended before attempting it"
 ],
 "local_import_closure_of_new_module": 28,
